    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0440" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6531/296: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-06T11:00:00+01:00">January 6, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 6—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Your No. 1, January 4, 3 p.m. I have done as instructed in last paragraph. Mr.
                        Suvich<anchor n="3" xml:id="d273-f1"/> said he had also received a cable
                    from Rosso in that sense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d273-f1" n="3" xml:id="d273-f1-content">
                <p>Fulvio Suvich, Under Secretary of State in Italian Ministry for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
